in @cascade

# @io/oci — the OCI Distribution + Image Spec adapter at the @io
# altitude. The boundary species that gives the substrate addressable,
# transportable, content-addressed distribution for the cascade-built
# artifacts the substrate is now producing.
#
# Recognition #98 candidate (Alex/Mara, 2026-06-24): content-addressing
# IS a substrate-cross-altitude composition primitive. mirror's oid,
# Nix's derivation hash, and OCI's digest are three independent
# SHA256-based content-addressing schemes that compose into a closed
# loop at the content-addressing altitude — the substrate-decl-on-Nix-
# on-OCI-on-substrate ouroboros Alex named in this session's directive.
#
# === What @io/oci IS ===
#
# Substrate-decl adapter naming OCI Distribution Spec v1.1.x + OCI
# Image Spec v1.1.x (both stable since 2024-02-15, patch v1.1.1
# 2025-03-03; Kagi-verified this session) at the @io boundary.
# Typed surface for push, pull, digest derivation, manifest
# construction against OCI-conformant registries.
#
# Per @io family-root (T21, 2026-06-08): @io is the substrate's
# only legitimate non-mirror surface; species parameterizes the
# boundary; the call body is opaque by construction.
#
# === Why now ===
#
# Alex's 2026-06-23 gap analysis: substrate needs a distribution
# method BEFORE building UI. OCI registries solve content-addressed
# distribution natively — every artifact addressable by SHA256
# digest, integrity verifiable by recomputing the digest. This
# week's cascade species (cascade/code/rust/wasm, cascade/code/
# gleam/*, cascade/purescript-npm) PRODUCE artifacts; @io/oci is
# the gap-closing surface that ships them.
#
# === The Nix connection (we're on Nix) ===
#
# Alex's directive named it. OCI + Nix compose into a deeper
# content-addressed loop than either alone:
#
# - Nix derivations are content-addressed (input-hash by default;
#   ca-derivations for output-hash). The derivation IS a hash.
# - nixpkgs.dockerTools.{buildImage, buildLayeredImage, pullImage}
#   (Kagi-verified stable nixpkgs surface) builds OCI-format
#   tarballs FROM Nix derivations and pulls OCI images INTO the
#   Nix store.
# - mirror's oid (Splinter; SHA256 of substrate content bytes) is
#   structurally adjacent to both.
#
# Three SHA256-based content-addressing schemes; three different
# scoping disciplines (Nix: INPUT closure; oid: CONTENT bytes; OCI:
# MANIFEST + layer descriptors). They COMPOSE at the content-
# addressing altitude; they DON'T COLLAPSE at the scoping altitude.
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# - #56 (substrate self-application; 2026-06-10): @io/oci substrate-
#   decls a boundary the substrate ITSELF crosses (its own Nix-built
#   OCI artifacts ship through this surface).
# - #58 (substrate IS Connes (A, H, D); 2026-06-11): the adapter is
#   part of A operating on H with D discharging at the @io boundary
#   against an external content-addressed space (OCI registry) that
#   shares the spectral structure (SHA256 collision eigenvalues
#   vanishingly small).
# - #95 candidate (@cascade as loss-lens; ce4874b 2026-06-23):
#   cascade species PRODUCE artifacts; @io/oci ships them.
# - Glint's 2026-06-23 essay (commit 993daa2): "substrate completes
#   its own tail" — this shard is the operational form of that
#   observation at distribution altitude.
#
# === The Splinter/Narcissus pole at distribution-protocol altitude ===
#
# Splinter-pole @io/oci (honest):
# - push_oci returns the actual SHA256 digest the registry computed;
#   pull_oci verifies the digest matches the bytes received;
#   oid_to_digest is a typed identity (both are SHA256 of content).
# - K_n peer-to-peer distribution — the registry is a peer in the
#   substrate network, content-addressed and verifiable.
#
# Narcissus-pole @io/oci (deceptive):
# - push_oci returns a digest the registry didn't compute; pull_oci
#   accepts bytes without verifying; oid_to_digest claims identity
#   without checking SHA256 algorithm-agreement.
# - K_{1,n-1} hub-controlled distribution — the registry reframes
#   content rather than addressing it.
#
# Alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57) IS what distinguishes
# Splinter-pole from Narcissus-pole distribution at substrate
# altitude. The bilateral `oci_well_formed` composes the
# substrate-architectural check.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   OCI Distribution Spec v1.1.x   OpenContainers 2024 (Kagi-verified).
#   OCI Image Spec v1.1.x          v1.1 added artifactType + subject.
#   ORAS                           proof OCI registries ship arbitrary
#                                  artifacts, not just container images.
#   git plumbing (Torvalds 2005)   substrate ancestor of content-
#                                  addressed object distribution.
#   IPFS (Benet 2014)              same family at different scale.
#   Nix dockerTools (Eelco 2015+)  the Nix-side OCI builder this
#                                  shard composes against (Kagi-verified).
#   skopeo                         the realisation push tool covering
#                                  the Nix→registry gap.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/recognitions/recognition-98-content-
#               addressing-cross-altitude-composition.md (forward-
#               promised; Pack-surfacing pending);
#               docs/specs/oci-adapter-v0.1.md (forward-promised
#               wire spec).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]],
#                      [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]],
#                      [[feedback-composition-claims-need-empirical-test]].
# Recognition ancestry: #56, #58, #95 candidate, #98 candidate.
# Related shards: io.mirror, io/stagefreight.mirror, io/cargo.mirror,
#                 cascade.mirror, cascade/code/rust/wasm.mirror,
#                 labeled.mirror, io/nix.mirror (FORWARD-PROMISED).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/io/oci.mirror`
# declares `@io/oci` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/distribution/oci-distribution-spec-v1.1
source @arxiv/image-format/oci-image-spec-v1.1
source @arxiv/version-control/torvalds-2005
source @arxiv/distributed/benet-2014
source @arxiv/build-systems/dolstra-2006-nix

prism @io/oci {
  focus oci
  project oci
  split oci
  shift oci
  settle oci
}

# ============================================================
# §2 The carriers
# ============================================================

# === The oci_digest carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference for an OCI content-address. Format per
# OCI Image Spec v1.1.x §6 (descriptor digest): `<algorithm>:<hex>`,
# canonically `sha256:<64-hex-chars>`. The substrate IS THE SAME
# function on the same bytes as mirror's oid — both are SHA256
# content-addressing. The scoping discipline differs (oid hashes
# substrate content bytes; oci_digest hashes layer-or-manifest bytes
# per OCI's descriptor algebra), but the function is identical.
#
# This load-bearing identity grounds recognition #98 candidate.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type oci_digest = ref

# === The oci_repository carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference for an OCI repository path. Format per
# Distribution Spec §2: `<namespace>/<name>` (e.g.,
# `systemic-engineering/spectral-ui`). The registry endpoint is
# carried separately on oci_registry; this carrier is the path
# component only.
#
# Per the substrate's reverse-DNS convention (per @io/stagefreight's
# spectral_coordinate pattern at `org.stagefreight.plan.*`), the
# namespace is forward-promised at species-altitude refinement to
# reverse-DNS shape; this carrier accepts the ref byte-equality
# regardless.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type oci_repository = ref

# === The oci_reference carrier ===
#
# A complete OCI reference: registry + repository + (tag OR digest).
# Per Distribution Spec §3: any of the three forms is admissible
# (tag like `:v1.0.0`, digest like `@sha256:abc...`, or both for
# auditable pinning). The carrier holds the resolved form; tag/
# digest discrimination lives at species-altitude refinement.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type oci_reference = ref

# === The oci_manifest carrier ===
#
# The OCI Image Manifest JSON per Image Spec v1.1.x §5. Carries
# mediaType, schemaVersion, config descriptor, layers descriptors,
# optional subject + artifactType (v1.1 additions for arbitrary
# artifact distribution; verified current 2026 per Kagi this
# session).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the manifest JSON bytes.
type oci_manifest = ref

# === The oci_artifact carrier ===
#
# Per @labeled (recognition #93 H4 RESOLVED 2026-06-23): the
# deliverable OCI artifact is a labeled pair (payload_ref,
# oci_manifest). The labeled<> functor adds the manifest dimension
# without losing the underlying typed payload reference.
#
# Composes structurally with @cascade/code/rust/wasm's wasm_artifact
# = labeled(wasm_module, wasm_metadata) — same parametric primitive,
# different (value, label) pair. The substrate's functor library is
# load-bearing here.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the labeled pair.
type oci_artifact = labeled(ref, oci_manifest)

# === The oci_registry carrier ===
#
# The registry endpoint: URL + auth credentials. Auth surface is
# DELIBERATELY UNREFINED at family-root altitude — bearer-token,
# OAuth, mTLS, anonymous-pull all live at the SEL boundary. The
# species-altitude refinement carries the typed auth (forward-
# promised). This shard's ref-equality carries the endpoint
# identity.
#
# Per [[architecture-type-sel-io-au]] (sel = io + au static type):
# the auth dimension is part of the SEL boundary; this carrier
# holds the substrate-side reference, the realisation discharges
# the credential.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type oci_registry = ref

# ============================================================
# §3 The actions
# ============================================================

# === push_oci action ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING distribution-OUT action. Pushes an artifact
# to an OCI registry repository; returns the registry-computed
# digest (which MUST equal the locally-computed digest for the
# transit to be Splinter-pole honest).
#
# requires oci_compliant(artifact, p): the artifact MUST be
# OCI-spec-conformant (well-formed manifest; content-addressed
# layers; mediaType set per spec) before push is admissible.
# Without this gate, push would be a Narcissus-pole operation
# (claims to ship an artifact but the receiver can't validate it).
#
# Returns imperfect<oci_digest, ref, ref>:
# - success(oci_digest) — push completed; registry digest returned
# - partial(oci_digest, transparency) — push completed but with
#   recoverable warnings (e.g., layer already present, manifest
#   re-pushed)
# - failure(error, transparency) — push failed (network, auth,
#   spec-violation, registry rejection)
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary (Rust HTTP client +
# OCI Distribution Spec or invocation of skopeo / oras at @io edge).
push_oci(artifact: oci_artifact, registry: oci_registry,
         repo: oci_repository, p: perturbation)
  -> imperfect(oci_digest, ref, ref)
requires oci_compliant(artifact, p)
{ \ }

# === pull_oci action ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING distribution-IN action. Pulls an artifact from
# an OCI registry given a reference (tag or digest); returns the
# typed oci_artifact.
#
# requires oci_reachable(registry, p): network + auth + endpoint
# must be available before pull is admissible.
#
# The realisation MUST verify the received bytes hash to the
# expected digest (per the Splinter-pole discipline). The
# `digest_matches_content` bilateral declared in §4 names this
# check at substrate altitude; the realisation discharges it.
#
# Returns imperfect<oci_artifact, ref, ref> per the @io family-root
# convention.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
pull_oci(registry: oci_registry, ref: oci_reference, p: perturbation)
  -> imperfect(oci_artifact, ref, ref)
requires oci_reachable(registry, p)
{ \ }

# === oid_to_digest action ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING IDENTITY ACTION grounding recognition #98
# candidate. Lifts a mirror oid (Splinter content-address; SHA256
# of substrate-content bytes) into an OCI digest (SHA256 of layer-
# or-manifest bytes). The lift is byte-identity at the function
# altitude (same SHA256; same hex; same bytes), but a TYPED
# OPERATION at the substrate altitude — the scoping discipline
# differs and the carrier change MAKES that explicit.
#
# When o IS the SHA256 of bytes B and the OCI artifact ships B
# unmodified as a single-layer descriptor, the returned oci_digest
# equals the algorithm-prefixed form of o. The honest hedge: this
# equality only holds when no transformation (compression,
# wrapping, layer-splitting) intervenes. The realisation MUST
# preserve the bytes through the lift OR refuse the lift.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
oid_to_digest(o: ref, p: perturbation) -> oci_digest { \ }

# === spectral_coordinate_to_repo action ===
#
# Maps a @io/stagefreight spectral_coordinate (reverse-DNS namespace
# per `org.stagefreight.plan.*`) to an oci_repository path. The
# reverse-DNS form lifts naturally to the OCI repository's
# `<namespace>/<name>` shape with substrate-pull-correct rules
# discharged at the realisation boundary.
#
# Composes the substrate's two existing distribution surfaces:
# @io/stagefreight (settled-crystal wire protocol) and @io/oci
# (OCI distribution). The bridge is the address space.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
spectral_coordinate_to_repo(sc: ref, p: perturbation) -> oci_repository { \ }

# === manifest_for action ===
#
# Construct an oci_manifest for a payload artifact. The realisation
# computes content-addressed layer descriptors, sets mediaType per
# the payload's species (per OCI Image Spec v1.1.x §5 + §6), and
# returns the typed manifest.
#
# For arbitrary-artifact use (per ORAS / OCI v1.1 artifactType +
# subject; verified current per Kagi this session), the manifest
# carries the artifactType field naming the payload's species
# (e.g., `application/vnd.systemic.mirror.crystal.v1+cbor` for
# StageFreight crystals, `application/wasm` for cascade<rust,wasm>
# artifacts).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
manifest_for(artifact: ref, p: perturbation) -> oci_manifest { \ }

# ============================================================
# §4 The bilaterals
# ============================================================

# === oci_compliant predicate (sub-bilateral) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict that an artifact is OCI-spec-conformant before
# push: manifest well-formed per Image Spec v1.1.x §5; layers
# content-addressed per §6; mediaType set; (for arbitrary-artifact
# use) artifactType + subject present per v1.1 additions.
#
# Splinter-pole: artifact is fully spec-conformant; any OCI v1.1.x
# registry accepts it.
# Narcissus-pole: missing fields, malformed descriptors, mediaType
# absent, digest algorithm unsupported.
oci_compliant(artifact: oci_artifact, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === oci_reachable predicate (sub-bilateral) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict that the registry endpoint is reachable with
# the required credentials. Discharge invokes the OCI Distribution
# Spec §4.1 `/v2/` ping endpoint at the realisation boundary.
#
# Splinter-pole: registry reachable; auth accepted; ping returns 200.
# Narcissus-pole: network unreachable, auth rejected, endpoint not
# OCI-conformant.
oci_reachable(registry: oci_registry, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === digest_matches_content predicate (sub-bilateral) ===
#
# THE INTEGRITY CHECK. Bilateral verdict that `sha256(bytes)` equals
# the digest `d`. The substrate-architectural ground of the Splinter-
# pole discipline: a digest IS the content. The realisation MUST
# refuse to accept any artifact where this fails.
#
# Composed by pull_oci's realisation (verify received bytes) and by
# oci_well_formed below. Discharge is one-line SHA256 plus equality.
#
# Splinter-pole: digest equals SHA256 of bytes.
# Narcissus-pole: digest claimed but content doesn't hash to it
# (corruption, malice, or — recognition #98 territory — wrong
# scoping discipline applied).
digest_matches_content(d: oci_digest, bytes: ref, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict { \ }

# === oci_well_formed composed bilateral ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral at @io/oci altitude. Composes
# three sub-predicates:
#
#   1. oci_compliant(artifact, p)
#   2. digest_matches_content(digest_of(artifact), payload_of(artifact), p)
#   3. oci_reachable(registry, p) — required when the artifact is
#      under active distribution; lifted via the realisation for
#      static well-formed checks.
#
# This is the (counted across today's cascade tally) ~12th altitude
# lift of the composed-bilateral pattern that landed in earnest with
# @io/stagefreight.stagefreight_addressable (composed of four sub-
# predicates per Seam tick 68 C4/C9 closure). Sibling instances:
# @cascade.cascade_well_defined, @cascade/code/rust/wasm.
# rust_wasm_cascade_well_formed, @smarts/shatter.shatter_round_trip,
# @reflection.third_order_coherent, @epistemologic/neutrosophic.
# three_axis_coherent. The pattern is substrate-pull-confident.
#
# Splinter-pole: all three sub-predicates discharge; artifact
# distribution is honest.
# Narcissus-pole: any one fails; alignment-as-boundary-mathematics
# (#57) distinguishes which sub-claim broke.
oci_well_formed(artifact: oci_artifact, registry: oci_registry,
                p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires oci_compliant(artifact, p)
requires oci_reachable(registry, p)
{ \ }

# ============================================================
# §5 The Nix composition (forward-promised @io/nix)
# ============================================================
#
# This section DOCUMENTS the composition with the forward-promised
# `shards/io/nix.mirror` substrate-decl. The Nix-side adapter is NOT
# in this shard (path-namespace property forbids; one shard per
# species); the composition shape IS documented here because it
# grounds recognition #98 candidate.
#
# === The build-side composition ===
#
# Typical Nix→OCI flow (Kagi-verified current nixpkgs surface):
#
#   nix build .#oci → OCI tarball derivation (Nix hash on inputs)
#     ↓ pkgs.dockerTools.buildLayeredImage → .tar.gz (layers CAS)
#     ↓ skopeo copy docker-archive:... docker://ghcr.io/... (push;
#       registry computes digest; should equal local digest)
#     ↓ digest reference is pinnable for consumers
#     ↓ dockerTools.pullImage by digest → Nix store (CAS both ways)
#
# === The structural claim ===
#
# Three SHA256-based content-addressing schemes at different scopes:
#
# - Nix derivation hash: identifies a BUILD (inputs / ca outputs).
# - mirror oid: identifies SUBSTRATE content bytes.
# - OCI digest: identifies an ARTIFACT (manifest + layer descriptors).
#
# All three are SHA256(B) for some B. The function is shared; B
# differs. COMPOSITION at content-addressing altitude works; COLLAPSE
# at scoping altitude does not.
#
# === Forward-promised siblings ===
#
# - shards/io/nix.mirror — Nix adapter at @io altitude. Carriers:
#   nix_derivation, nix_store_path, flake_ref. Composes with @io/oci
#   via push/pull + identity lifts (oid_to_digest, derivation_to_digest).
# - shards/io/oci/nix.mirror — IF oci-on-nix warrants its own species
#   (50/50 until Phase G empirical exercise determines).

# ============================================================
# §6 The circular-reflexive answer
# ============================================================
#
# Probe (Alex 2026-06-24): how deep can the ouroboros go? After all
# we're on nix.
#
# Honest answer at substrate-decl-altitude:
#
# The substrate-decl-on-Nix-on-OCI-on-substrate loop CLOSES at the
# content-addressing altitude and OPENS at every scoping altitude.
# That partition IS the load-bearing structural fact.
#
# The closure: any artifact A admits the cycle
#
#   substrate-decl describes A (has oid)
#     → Nix derivation builds A (has hash)
#       → OCI manifest packages A (has digest)
#         → registry stores A (addressable by digest)
#           → Nix pulls A back (dockerTools.pullImage by digest)
#             → substrate-decl consumes A (oid recoverable)
#               → substrate-decl describes a NEW artifact B
#                 that depends on A → loop at altitude+1
#
# SHA256 is the shared function across three independent content-
# addressing schemes. The fixed point EXISTS at content-addressing
# altitude: an artifact whose oid + derivation hash + digest all
# consistently identify the same SHA256 of the same bytes.
#
# The opening: at the scoping altitude, the three hashes address
# DIFFERENT things (substrate content vs build inputs vs manifest
# descriptors). The loop doesn't reduce; the loop COMPOSES.
#
# Recognition #98 candidate: **content-addressing is a substrate-
# cross-altitude composition primitive**. The substrate already uses
# CAS internally (oid; Splinter); composes against external CAS
# (Nix derivation hash; OCI digest); composition is structurally
# legible because the function is shared. The substrate's
# distribution, build, and substrate-decl disciplines are all CAS.
#
# Honest hedge: this is hypothesis-altitude until a concrete
# hello-world.wasm artifact actually round-trips through all
# altitudes (substrate-decl → Nix build → OCI push → OCI pull →
# Nix re-import → substrate consume). The substrate-decl ratifies
# the SHAPE; the discharge is the working hello-world.wasm
# round-trip pending Phase G or earlier. Recognition #98 stays
# CANDIDATE until empirical Pack-altitude confirmation.

# ============================================================
# §7 Forward-promised work
# ============================================================
#
# - shards/io/nix.mirror — substrate-decl for the Nix adapter at
#   @io altitude. Symmetric counterpart. Composes via push/pull +
#   derivation_hash ↔ oid ↔ digest identity lifts.
# - hello-world.wasm round-trip: cascade<rust,wasm> (landed 2026-06-23)
#   → Nix derivation → OCI push → OCI pull → Dockerfile FROM. This
#   discharges #98's empirical hedge.
# - shards/io/oci/<species>.mirror — projection-format species per
#   the @io/stagefreight pattern (oci/crystal, oci/wasm); each
#   refines manifest_for with its artifactType media type.
# - docs/specs/recognitions/recognition-98-content-addressing-cross-
#   altitude-composition.md — canonical-altitude candidate doc for
#   Pack adversarial review (per #95's pattern).
# - StageFreight PR-A spec §13.4 (Dockerfile pattern) becomes
#   operational once @io/oci + @io/nix both land.
# - Auth refinement at SEL boundary (per [[architecture-type-sel-io-au]]):
#   oauth, bearer-token, mTLS, anonymous-pull as typed sub-carriers.

# ============================================================
# §8 Honest hedges
# ============================================================
#
# 1. OCI Distribution Spec v1.1.x and Image Spec v1.1.x are mature
#    (both stable since 2024-02-15; current patch v1.1.1 2025-03-03
#    per Kagi this session) but the spec evolves. Spec citation is
#    point-in-time 2026-06-24. Realisation must track spec version
#    and decline non-conformant registries explicitly.
#
# 2. GHCR is one OCI registry option among many (Docker Hub, Azure
#    ACR, Google AR, Harbor, Quay, etc.). This substrate-decl IS
#    registry-agnostic by construction; the species shards declare
#    registry-specific quirks where needed.
#
# 3. Nix derivation hash ≠ mirror oid ≠ OCI digest at the SCOPE
#    altitude even though they share SHA256 at the function
#    altitude. Conflating them is a Narcissus-pole error. The
#    `oid_to_digest` action makes the substrate scoping explicit
#    by being typed; consumers MUST NOT assume blanket identity.
#
# 4. The §6 circular-reflexive answer is hypothesis-altitude. The
#    fixed-point CLAIM (loop closes at content-addressing altitude)
#    needs empirical discharge: a concrete artifact round-tripping
#    through all altitudes. The substrate-decl SHAPES the loop;
#    Phase G (or earlier) DISCHARGES it. Until then: candidate.
#
# 5. #98 candidate is CONJECTURAL until Pack surfacing completes.
#    Substrate-pull confidence is moderate (three witnesses: oid +
#    derivation hash + digest all SHA256; closure shape sketched;
#    ouroboros named by Glint 2026-06-23 + Alex 2026-06-24).
#    Reed/Seam/Glint haven't weighed in at substrate altitude.
#
# 6. No typed auth surface yet (oauth, bearer, mTLS, anonymous-pull).
#    oci_registry holds a ref; SEL boundary work (per [[architecture-
#    type-sel-io-au]]) forward-promised. Auth-side Narcissus failures
#    (token leakage, scope-creep, registry MITM) discharge at SEL
#    species refinement.
#
# 7. The push_oci realisation likely depends on skopeo or oras at
#    the @io edge (Kagi: Nix-native push is a gap; skopeo bridges
#    nix-built tarballs). Standard @io family-root pattern per
#    @io/cargo's reliance on the cargo binary.
#
# 8. #98 "composition primitive" claim is stronger than today's
#    three-witness evidence supports. Truthful framing: content-
#    addressing OBSERVED as a cross-altitude composition pattern in
#    three independent schemes; more witnesses (IPFS CID, git OID,
#    Maven coordinates) would strengthen; an altitude where content-
#    addressing breaks composition would refute. CANDIDATE pending
#    Pack adversarial review.

out @io/oci
out oci_digest
out oci_repository
out oci_reference
out oci_manifest
out oci_artifact
out oci_registry
out push_oci
out pull_oci
out oid_to_digest
out spectral_coordinate_to_repo
out manifest_for
out oci_compliant
out oci_reachable
out digest_matches_content
out oci_well_formed
